  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Will it be possible in the future for VRChat to expose the local rotation of the head (left-right, up-down, and side-side) and eyes (left-right, up-down) as Fload parameters for the Animator?\n\nSo that fully left would be -1 and fully right 1, fully up would be 1 and fully down would be -1, and tilting to the left -1 and to the right 1?\n\nSame with eyes, fully left -1, fully right 1, fully up 1 and fully down -1?\n\nThat would be better for things like ears tilting with the direction of the head and twisting with the direction of the eyes, possible now by using contacts or physbone colliders. \n\nDoing that with built in parameters driven by VRChat would be better because that would save the physbone/contacts count in avatars that might have this feature.\n\nHere's a video demonstrating that using physbone collider:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/LRZ-7HS2Mhg",
